    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "Find $p$ so that $(x-p)$ is a factor of $4x^3-(10p-1)x^2+(6p^2-5)x+6$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$p=2$ or $p=3$.",
      "worked": "By the factor theorem, $P(p)=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(p)&=4p^3-(10p-1)p^2+(6p^2-5)p+6\\\\0&=4p^3-10p^3+p^2+6p^3-5p+6\\\\0&=p^2-5p+6\\\\0&=(p-2)(p-3).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $p=2$ or $p=3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
